## 11. MVP vs. Production Version Comparison

The transformation from the MVP prototype to the Production SaaS platform involves significant architectural and functional improvements:

| Dimension | MVP Prototype 🧪 | Production SaaS Platform 💎 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Authentication** | Basic local storage tokens; simple role redirects. | Secure HttpOnly cookies with CSRF protection and token expiration handling. |
| **Team Size** | Single-user projects. | Dynamic team invitation system supporting up to 5 members. |
| **Workspace** | Local text editor placeholder. | Collaborative rich text workspace with autosave and conflict resolution. |
| **Grading** | Manual input forms. | Dynamic 100-mark scoring combining automated data metrics and manual rubrics. |
| **File Uploads** | Basic uploads without file type verification. | Highly secure uploads validating MIME-types, file sizes, and hashing names. |
| **Real-time Sync** | Manual browser refreshes required. | Immediate updates for Kanban, chat, and alerts powered by WebSockets. |
| **Background Jobs** | None; all calculations run on request. | Automated Redis queues handling deadline alerts, late penalties, and GitHub polling. |
| **Analytics** | Hardcoded static charts. | Fully dynamic Recharts dashboards querying indexed MySQL database views. |
| **Logging** | Console logging. | Centralized logging using Winston. Separates debug files from system errors. |
| **Security** | Open CORS policies; HTTP connections. | Strict CORS whitelisting, Helmet security headers, Let's Encrypt SSL certificates. |

